<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        The items are given through Items, and the one the user picks is the Value. The Label names the list for everyone.
        Tab into the list and use the arrow keys, or type the first letters of a fruit.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Fruit" Items="basicItems" @bind-Value="basicValue" />
        <div>Value: <b>@basicValue</b></div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="MultiSelect" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
    <div>
        With MultiSelect the user picks several items, which are the Values. The arrow keys only move; Space, Enter or a
        click adds the item to the selection or takes it out.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Fruits" Items="basicItems" MultiSelect @bind-Values="multiValues" />
        <div>Values: <b>@string.Join(", ", multiValues ?? [])</b></div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Description & icon" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
    <div>An item can carry an icon before its text and a Description under it.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Shipping" Items="iconItems" DefaultValue="@("standard")" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
    <div>IsDisabled keeps the user off an item, which the keyboard passes by; Disabled keeps the user off the whole list.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Some disabled" Items="disabledItems" TItem="BitListBoxItem<string>" TValue="string" />
        <BitListBox Label="Disabled" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("banana")" Disabled />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="ReadOnly" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
    <div>A ReadOnly list box can be read and moved through with the keyboard, but its selection cannot be changed.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Read only" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("cherry")" ReadOnly />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="MaxHeight" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
    <div>
        MaxHeight is the height past which the list scrolls. The keyboard keeps the item it is on in view, and typing the
        start of a name goes straight to it.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Country" Items="countryItems" MaxHeight="12rem" @bind-Value="countryValue" />
        <div>Value: <b>@countryValue</b></div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Validation" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7">
    <div>
        The list box binds to an EditForm and is validated with it, in both modes: ShowValidationMessage shows the messages
        of the field under the list. ErrorMessage and Invalid mark it invalid from the page itself.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>
        <EditForm Model="validationModel" OnValidSubmit="() => validationResult = validationModel.ToString()">
            <DataAnnotationsValidator />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitListBox Label="Fruit (required)" Items="basicItems" @bind-Value="validationModel.Fruit" Required ShowValidationMessage />
                <BitListBox Label="Fruits (at least two)" Items="basicItems" MultiSelect @bind-Values="validationModel.Fruits" ShowValidationMessage />
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton ButtonType="BitButtonType.Submit">Submit</BitButton>
        </EditForm>
        <br />
        <div>Submitted: <b>@validationResult</b></div>
        <br />
        <div class="example-box">
            <BitListBox Label="With an error message" Items="basicItems" TItem="BitListBoxItem<string>" TValue="string" ErrorMessage="This fruit is out of season." />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Events" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
    <div>OnSelectItem runs when an item is selected, and in multi select mode OnDeselectItem when one is taken out.</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Items="basicItems" TItem="BitListBoxItem<string>" TValue="string"
                    AriaLabel="Fruits"
                    MultiSelect
                    OnSelectItem="HandleOnSelectItem"
                    OnDeselectItem="HandleOnDeselectItem" />
        <div>Last event: <b>@eventsLog</b></div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="External Icons" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
    <div>The Icon of an item takes the CSS classes of any icon library, such as FontAwesome or Bootstrap Icons.</div>
    <br />
    <div>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/7.0.1/css/all.min.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css" />
        <div class="example-box">
            <BitListBox Label="FontAwesome" Items="externalIconItems1" DefaultValue="@("car")" />
            <BitListBox Label="Bootstrap Icons" Items="externalIconItems2" DefaultValue="@("bike")" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10">
    <div>
        Style and Class reach the root, the Style and Class of an item reach that item, and Styles and Classes reach each
        part by name. The selected colors are also the public --bit-ListBox-* variables.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Label="Style" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("banana")" Style="--bit-ListBox-selected-color: tomato; --bit-ListBox-selected-background: #ff63471f;" />
        <BitListBox Label="Class" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("banana")" Class="custom-class" />
        <BitListBox Label="Item's Style & Class" Items="styleClassItems" TItem="BitListBoxItem<string>" TValue="string" />
        <BitListBox Label="Styles & Classes"
                    Items="basicItems"
                    MultiSelect
                    DefaultValues="@(["apple", "cherry"])"
                    Styles="@(new() { List = "border-radius: 0.75rem;", Text = "font-style: italic;" })"
                    Classes="@(new() { SelectedItem = "custom-selected" })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example11CsharpCode" Id="example11">
    <div>Use BitListBox in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
    <br />
    <div dir="rtl" class="example-box">
        <BitListBox Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Label="میوه" Items="rtlItems" DefaultValue="@("banana")" />
        <BitListBox Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Label="میوه‌ها" Items="rtlItems" MultiSelect DefaultValues="@(["apple", "cherry"])" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>
